\\outl0\\strokewidth0 \\strokec2 # Missingness Analysis\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\\
\
\\f0\\b \\cf2 \\cb3 \\strokec2 ## Why it matters\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf4 \\cb3 The validation workbook contains structural missingness: many columns (e.g., MRI-specific\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 elements like \\cf2 \\strokec2 `extent_status_*`\\cf4 \\strokec4  and \\cf2 \\strokec2 `additional_enhancement_mri_status_*`\\cf4 \\strokec4 ) are absent for\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 cases where the relevant imaging modality was not performed. Before drawing conclusions\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 from accuracy estimates, it is important to understand whether this missingness is random\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 or systematic.\\cb1 \\\
\\\
\\cb3 If missing annotations are \
\\f0\\b \\cf5 \\strokec5 **not**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\strokec4  random (MNAR), accuracy estimates computed over\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 source-present cases may be biased toward or against cases with a particular profile.\\cb1 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\
\\f0\\b \\cf2 \\cb3 \\strokec2 ## Missingness mechanisms\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf4 \\cb3 | Mechanism | Definition |\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 |---|---|\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 | \
\\f0\\b \\cf5 \\strokec5 **MCAR**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\strokec4  (Missing Completely At Random) | Missingness is independent of any variable (observed or unobserved). Safe to use complete-case analysis. |\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 | \
\\f0\\b \\cf5 \\strokec5 **MAR**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\strokec4  (Missing At Random) | Missingness depends on observed variables but not on the unobserved value itself. Bias can be corrected by conditioning on the observed variables. |\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 | \
\\f0\\b \\cf5 \\strokec5 **MNAR**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\strokec4  (Missing Not At Random) | Missingness depends on the unobserved value. The most problematic scenario - complete-case analysis may be biased. |\\cb1 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\
\\f0\\b \\cf2 \\cb3 \\strokec2 ## Classification utility\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\
\\f0\\b \\cf5 \\cb3 \\strokec5 **File**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\strokec4 : \\cf2 \\strokec2 `src/missing_data_classification.py`\\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf4 \\cb3 The utility classifies each column of an input dataset independently using three tests:\\cb1 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\
\\f0\\b \\cf2 \\cb3 \\strokec2 ### 1. Little's MCAR test\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf4 \\cb3 A global chi-squared test of whether the missing-data pattern is consistent with MCAR.\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 If significant (p < 0.05), the dataset is classified as \
\\f0\\b \\cf5 \\strokec5 **Not MCAR**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\strokec4  overall.\\cb1 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\
\\f0\\b \\cf2 \\cb3 \\strokec2 ### 2. MAR detection - point-biserial correlations\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf4 \\cb3 For each column with missing values, a missingness indicator (0/1) is correlated with\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 all other numeric columns using the point-biserial coefficient. If |r| exceeds the\\cb1 \\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf2 \\cb3 \\strokec2 `--mar-threshold`\\cf4 \\strokec4  (default 0.1) for any pair, the column is flagged \
\\f0\\b \\cf5 \\strokec5 **MAR**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\strokec4 .\\cb1 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\
\\f0\\b \\cf2 \\cb3 \\strokec2 ### 3. MNAR heuristic - KS test\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf4 \\cb3 For columns remaining after the MAR check, a two-sample Kolmogorov-Smirnov test compares\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 the distribution of each numeric variable in observed vs. missing subgroups. A significant\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 result suggests the missingness depends on the value itself (MNAR).\\cb1 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\
\\f0\\b \\cf2 \\cb3 \\strokec2 ## Running the classification\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf4 \\cb3 ```bash\\cb1 \\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf6 \\cb3 \\strokec6 python\\cf7 \\cb3 \\strokec7  \\cf8 \\cb3 \\strokec8 src/missing_data_classification.py\\cf7 \\cb3 \\strokec7  \\cf9 \\strokec9 \\\\\\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf7 \\cb3 \\strokec7   --input data/raw/merged_llm_summary_validation_datasheet.xlsx \\\\\\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\cf7 \\cb3 \\strokec7   \\cf10 \\strokec10 --outdir\\cf7 \\strokec7  \\cf8 \\cb3 \\strokec8 data/processed\\cf7 \\cb3 \\strokec7  \\cf9 \\strokec9 \\\\\\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\cf7 \\cb3 \\strokec7   --coerce-na\\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf4 \\cb3 ```\\cb1 \\\
\\\
\\cb3 The \\cf2 \\strokec2 `--coerce-na`\\cf4 \\strokec4  flag is required for this dataset because placeholder strings\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 (\\cf2 \\strokec2 `'na'`\\cf4 \\strokec4 , \\cf2 \\strokec2 `'NA'`\\cf4 \\strokec4 , \\cf2 \\strokec2 `'N/A'`\\cf4 \\strokec4 ) appear alongside true blanks. Without it, affected columns\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 are read as \\cf2 \\strokec2 `object`\\cf4 \\strokec4  dtype and silently excluded from the numerical tests.\\cb1 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\
\\f0\\b \\cf2 \\cb3 \\strokec2 ## Known results for this dataset\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf4 \\cb3 Running the utility with \\cf2 \\strokec2 `--coerce-na`\\cf4 \\strokec4  on the 200-case validation workbook produces:\\cb1 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf6 \\cb3 \\strokec6 -\\cf4 \\strokec4  \
\\f0\\b \\cf5 \\strokec5 **Little's test**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\strokec4 : p ~ 0 - the dataset is \
\\f0\\b \\cf5 \\strokec5 **Not MCAR**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\cf6 \\cb3 \\strokec6 -\\cf4 \\strokec4  \
\\f0\\b \\cf5 \\strokec5 **All 24 columns with missing data**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\strokec4 : classified as \
\\f0\\b \\cf5 \\strokec5 **MAR**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\cf6 \\cb3 \\strokec6 -\\cf4 \\strokec4  \
\\f0\\b \\cf5 \\strokec5 **MNAR**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\strokec4 : no columns flagged\\cb1 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf4 \\cb3 This is consistent with the interpretation that missingness is driven by imaging modality\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 and procedure type (structural MAR), not by the value of the missing finding itself. The\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 accuracy estimates are therefore not expected to be substantially biased by the missing\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 data pattern.\\cb1 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\
\\f0\\b \\cf2 \\cb3 \\strokec2 ## Outputs\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf4 \\cb3 Written to \\cf2 \\strokec2 `data/processed/`\\cf4 \\strokec4  (git-ignored):\\cb1 \\\
\\\
